  <wpt lat="35.116700" lon="-82.600000">
    <name>Ceasar's Head State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; no prior coordinate (Nominatim returned no result)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.692500" lon="-82.384722">
    <name>Craggy Gardens</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; moved ~1km to the Wikidata point</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.018900" lon="-85.339500">
    <name>Ruby Falls</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate for the Tennessee Ruby Falls within ~30m</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.777500" lon="-83.693600">
    <name>Natural Bridge State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; moved ~0.55km to the Wikidata point for Natural Bridge State Resort Park</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.875670" lon="-81.077598">
    <name>New River Gorge National River</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Glen Jean, WV named in the query (a real town within the park, near its south end); the park's overall Wikidata centroid (wikidata:Q7011245) is ~9.5km further north near the New River Gorge Bridge, but the query specifies Glen Jean; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Grandview Visitor Center (NPS), the nearest visitor center to the display point, which sits in the gorge near Prince rather than in Glen Jean (osm:node/8913641237)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.029900" lon="-78.479000">
    <name>Monticello Wine Trail</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; no prior coordinate (Nominatim returned no result); the wine trail is a spread-out regional brand covering dozens of wineries in Albemarle County with no single fixed location, so the Charlottesville city center (the trail's namesake hub) is used as the best available reference point</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.768826" lon="-76.206767">
    <name>St. Michaels Inn</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real St Michaels, MD address given in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="38.766700" lon="-75.095800">
    <name>Cape Henlopen State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; moved ~0.76km to the Wikidata point; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Seaside Nature Center, the park visitor center (osm:way/366333732, Delaware State Parks)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.915541" lon="-74.180529">
    <name>Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate within ~35m</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.576246" lon="-72.642729">
    <name>Brownstone Exploration &amp; Discovery Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real Portland, CT address given in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.489983" lon="-71.313771">
    <name>Newport</name>
    <desc>Newport</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.356311" lon="-68.215479">
    <name>Acadia National Park</name>
    <desc>drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Sand Beach lot on the Park Loop Road, the same drive point as the identical query in major-landmarks row 28 and the national-parks page row 14 (2015 Google matrix evidence there)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.271560" lon="-71.540182">
    <name>Cog Railway</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real base station address given in the query; Wikidata's point for the railway (wikidata:Q458111) is ~16.5km east near the summit terminus of the same line</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.430062" lon="-71.976367">
    <name>Northeast Kingdom</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; close to St Johnsbury, VT named in the query; the Northeast Kingdom itself is a huge multi-county region, so its Wikidata centroid (wikidata:Q3643161, ~23km away) is far less specific than the given address</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.614391" lon="-72.870186">
    <name>66 Thunder Mountain Rd</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real Charlemont, MA address given in the query (Berkshire East / Zoar Outdoor area); drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Berkshire East main parking lot at the end of Thunder Mountain Rd (osm:way/255823444); the address point sat on the ski slopes</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.084841" lon="-79.070179">
    <name>Niagara Falls</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate for the falls itself (not the city) within ~50m</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="40.430903" lon="-80.010331">
    <name>Mount Washington</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real Mount Washington neighborhood of Pittsburgh, PA given in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.110003" lon="-84.537802">
    <name>Cincinnati Museum Center</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the real address (1301 Western Ave, Cincinnati, at Union Terminal) within a few meters</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.658749" lon="-87.055250">
    <name>Indiana Dunes State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the given address in Chesterton, IN; Wikidata's point (wikidata:Q598933) is for the broader Indiana Dunes National Park, ~1.3km away</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.878738" lon="-87.635961">
    <name>Willis Tower</name>
    <desc>Willis Tower</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.118791" lon="-90.778872">
    <name>Maquoketa Caves State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate within ~85m</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.423714" lon="-86.623827">
    <name>Pictured Rocks National Lakeshore</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Munising, MI named in the query (the park's west-end gateway town); Wikidata's park centroid (wikidata:Q3382575) is ~28km east near Grand Marais, the other end of this large park</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.813015" lon="-90.820528">
    <name>Apostle Islands National Lakeshore</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches the given address (415 Washington Ave, Bayfield, WI), the mainland visitor center for the islands; Wikidata's point (wikidata:Q2855854) is out on the islands themselves, ~20km away</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.069292" lon="-91.108192">
    <name>Boundary Waters Canoe Area Wilderness</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls within the actual wilderness area near Ely, MN, even though the query names Duluth (~150km south) as an access city; kept since it correctly represents the named wilderness itself, per the pipeline's simplified-query fallback; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Moose Lake public water access (BWCAW Entry Point 25, the busiest Ely-area entry point, Fernberg Rd east of Ely; osm:node/7763480115, USFS); the display point is inside the roadless wilderness</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="46.895449" lon="-103.381578">
    <name>Painted Canyon Visitor Center</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; close to the I-94 Exit 32 / Belfield, ND area named in the query; no Wikidata entity for this specific visitor center</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="43.527106" lon="-102.361663">
    <name>Badlands National Park</name>
    <desc>drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Ben Reifel Visitor Center at Cedar Pass, the main park visitor center (osm:way/36131704); the display point is in the South Unit backcountry</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="41.589261" lon="-103.104643">
    <name>Courthouse Rock</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~1.3km of the Wikidata point for this Nebraska rock formation (wikidata:Q34866482)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.107033" lon="-110.259166">
    <name>Yellowstone National Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls within Yellowstone National Park (a ~9,000 km2 park with no address given beyond its own ZIP code); Wikidata's park centroid (wikidata:Q351) is ~58km away, also within the park; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: West Thumb Geyser Basin parking (osm:relation/15912347); Google placed its Yellowstone National Park pin at about 44.428,-110.588, 1.7 km from West Thumb, so a 2015 route to this query most plausibly ended on the Grand Loop here; the display point is roadless backcountry south of Yellowstone Lake</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.511685" lon="-110.579741">
    <name>Paradise Valley</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls within the Paradise Valley, MT area along the Yellowstone River; no Wikidata entity for this valley; could not obtain a more precise geocode without Nominatim</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.596006" lon="-114.402162">
    <name>Shoshone Falls</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; matches Wikidata coordinate for Shoshone Falls within ~130m</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.643735" lon="-121.105892">
    <name>Columbia River Gorge</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls within the actual scenic Columbia River Gorge near Hood River; note the given address (George, WA, home of the Gorge Amphitheatre) is not actually in the river gorge and appears to be a mix-up in the original source, so the resolved point for the gorge itself is kept</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="42.941523" lon="-122.098771">
    <name>Crater Lake</name>
    <desc>drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Rim Village Visitor Center, the main car-reachable lake overlook (osm:way/146403404, wikidata:Q36050721); the display point is in the lake</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.088541" lon="-120.050353">
    <name>Lake Tahoe</name>
    <desc>drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Sand Harbor Visitor Center, Lake Tahoe Nevada State Park, the main Nevada-shore public access (osm:way/576484412); the display point is mid-lake</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.585240" lon="-121.884203">
    <name>CA-1</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls along CA-1 near Monterey, CA as named in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.782488" lon="-113.072145">
    <name>Frazier Wells</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; falls in the correct area of northern Arizona (Hualapai Reservation, near Grand Canyon West) as named in the query; no Wikidata entity for this place</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.570795" lon="-112.185594">
    <name>Bryce Canyon National Park</name>
    <desc>drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Bryce Canyon Visitor Center on UT 63, the main visitor center (NPS API, same as the national-parks page row 28)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="39.072211" lon="-107.188938">
    <name>Marble</name>
    <desc>Marble</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.169761" lon="-106.372690">
    <name>Sandia Mountains</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~8km of the Wikidata point for the Sandia Mountains (wikidata:Q1476263), reasonable for a query with only a ZIP code and no specific address on a large mountain range</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="29.165470" lon="-103.612120">
    <name>Santa Elena Canyon</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; Nominatim's simplified-query result was near San Antonio, TX, about 700km from the actual Santa Elena Canyon in Big Bend National Park named in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.500600" lon="-96.972200">
    <name>Chickasaw National Recreation Area</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; moved ~5.7km to the Wikidata point, closer to the Sulphur, OK visitor center address given in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="37.367264" lon="-96.188604">
    <name>Elk Falls</name>
    <desc>Elk Falls</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="36.625554" lon="-93.411194">
    <name>Table Rock Lake</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~12km of the Wikidata point for Table Rock Lake (wikidata:Q7332040), both plausible on this ~70km-long lake given no address in the query</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="35.890980" lon="-93.440416">
    <name>Whitaker Point Trail (Hawksbill Crag)</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~2.2km of the well-known Hawksbill Crag overlook in the Ozark National Forest; no Wikidata entity for this specific trail/overlook; drive point fixed 2026-09-26: Whitaker Point (Hawksbill Crag) trailhead parking on Cave Mountain Rd (osm:way/1375111102)</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="34.600939" lon="-88.178295">
    <name>Tishomingo State Park</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; within ~1.1km of the Wikidata point for the park</desc>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="30.534628" lon="-91.739257">
    <name>Atchafalaya National Wildpark Refuge</name>
    <desc>verified 2026-09-26; no prior coordinate (Nominatim returned no result); used the Wikidata point for the refuge, which is roughly 20km from the Hwy 190/I-10 interchange named in the query -- could not obtain a precise address-level geocode without Nominatim</desc>
  </wpt>
